   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>The quadratic function <span data-math=\"y=-(x-2)(x+3)\">y=-(x-2)(x+3)</span> is graphed below.</p>\n<p><img height=\"254\" src=\"exercises/media/c3ec52d0642fc220.jpg\" width=\"249\" alt=\"A graph displays a downward-opening parabola, symmetric about the y-axis, with its vertex at (0, 6). The curve passes through approximately (-2.5, 0) and (2.5, 0).\"></p>\n<p>What are all of the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-intercepts?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1331971,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x =6\">x =6</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1331972,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = - 3\">x = - 3</span>, <span data-math=\"x = 2\">x = 2</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1331973,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = 2, x = 6\">x = 2, x = 6</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1331974,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = - 3\">x = - 3</span>"
    }
